{# The site-wide "How this works" page (hosting/pages.py).

   Election-agnostic, so its page head carries no eyebrow and its footer no
   source panel; its band highlights the About nav entry. #}
{% extends 'base.html.j2' %}
{% block head_meta %}
  {{ shell.social_meta(document_title, page_description, canonical_url) }}
{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
  <a class="skip-link" href="#about-main">Skip to content</a>
  <div class="page">
    <header>
      {{ shell.band(guide_href=current_path, sources_href=current_path ~ 'sources/', compare_href=compare_href, corrections_href=corrections_href, current='about') }}
      <div class="page-band-rule"></div>
    </header>
    {%+ call shell.page_head('How this works', mode='measured') %}{{ page_description }}{% endcall +%}
    <main id="about-main" class="narrow-main">

      <section aria-labelledby="what-this-is">
        <h2 id="what-this-is">What this guide tells you</h2>
        <p>This guide brings together endorsements published by progressive and left-of-center
          organizations. The agreement percentage shows how much those organizations agree.</p>
        <p>We do not independently vet candidates or predict who will win. This is an independent
          guide, not an official voter pamphlet.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="how-the-numbers-work">
        <h2 id="how-the-numbers-work">How the numbers work</h2>
        <p>Each organization gets one point per race. If it endorses more than one candidate,
          that point splits evenly among them unless the organization states its own split.</p>
        <p>The percentage is the leading choice's share of those points. The source count beside
          it tells you how many organizations contributed; neither number is a quality rating of the
          candidate.</p>
        <p>Silence, an explicit "no endorsement," and races a source did not cover are counted
          separately. They never enter a candidate's share. The source count keeps the size of
          the sample visible.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="which-sources-count">
        <h2 id="which-sources-count">Which sources count</h2>
        <p>Legislative-district organizations count on the broader races their district covers, but
          only on their own district's legislative contests.</p>
        <p>Some tracked organizations are related &mdash; a state and local chapter of the same
          group, for example. These relationships are disclosed rather than deduplicated: each
          separately governed organization keeps its own full vote.</p>
        <p>The Seattle Times is tracked only as a comparison. It contributes no points, and
          the Endorsements page does not show it. The Sources page documents it, and
          the Comparisons page is where you can put it beside the aggregate.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="compare-sources">
        <h2 id="compare-sources">Compare sources</h2>
        <p>The {% if compare_href %}<a href="{{ compare_href }}">Comparisons page</a>{% else %}Comparisons page{% endif %}
          puts up to three columns side by side for every race. A column can
          show all sources together, one organization, or a category of organizations.</p>
        <p>The first column is the reference for the differences highlighted across the row. Category columns
          give each member organization equal weight, while sources such as The Seattle Times are
          shown only for comparison and never change the overall result.</p>
        <p>Share the page's address to share its columns and filters. With the same data version,
          the link restores the same view. If a link is outdated or unrecognized, the page explains
          why it has returned to the default view.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="why-ballot-varies">
        <h2 id="why-ballot-varies">Why your ballot may look different</h2>
        <p>Exact ballot contents vary by voter registration address. This guide covers the Seattle
          races we tracked for this election; your ballot may not include all of them, and may
          include a race this guide doesn&rsquo;t cover.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="choices-anonymous">
        <h2 id="choices-anonymous">Are my choices anonymous?</h2>
        <p>Your source selection lives entirely in this page's address. Nothing is stored anywhere
          else, and the site has no account or profile connected to your choices. Anyone you share
          that address with can see the selection it contains.</p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="source-panel">
        <h2 id="source-panel">When the guide changes</h2>
        <p>The organizations we count are registered before scoring begins. We do not change
          that list to fit an outcome. A missed or misclassified source belongs in a later,
          explicitly versioned list. Each release preserves the exact list's ID and hash.</p>
        <p>Every change to the published aggregate or a race page belongs in
          {% if corrections_href %}<a href="{{ corrections_href }}">Updates</a>{% else %}Updates{% endif %}.
          That includes new endorsements, corrections, withdrawals, and revised results.
          A changed source count, percentage, or endorsement list gets an entry even when the
          leading choice stays the same.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="verify-it">
        <h2 id="verify-it">Verify it yourself</h2>
        <p>Each source row links to the organization's own endorsement page or document.
          Follow that link to check a recorded endorsement.</p>
        <p>Organizations can update their own endorsements after we capture them, so a source's
          current page may drift from what a guide recorded; use the same evidence links to confirm
          the evidence behind any race.</p>
        <p>The footer gives the data and site update dates. Its data-version link opens the
          release manifest; its site-revision link opens the exact code that built the page.</p>
        <p><a href="{{ current_path }}release-status.json">Current release status</a> and
          <a href="{{ current_path }}release-manifest.json">release manifest</a> are public JSON
          files identifying the current guide, its source list, and its published files.
          The complete decision ledger, source metadata, and validation
          reports for every release are published in the
          <a href="{{ project_url }}"{{ external_link_attributes }}>project's source repository</a>,
          alongside the code that produced them.</p>
        <p>Past guides remain published at their own permanent addresses in the
          <a href="/e/">guide archive</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="election-dates-in-your-calendar">
        <h2 id="election-dates-in-your-calendar">Election dates in your calendar</h2>
        <p>Subscribe to <a href="/calendar.ics">the election calendar</a> and your own calendar app
          will remind you when ballots are mailed, when this guide publishes, and when ballots are
          due. Your app controls reminders and checks for changes on its own schedule.
          A moved date updates the existing event.</p>
        <p>The calendar is a static file. There is no account, notification service, or record
          of who subscribed. It carries dates only; endorsements stay in the guide.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="report-a-correction">
        <h2 id="report-a-correction">Send a correction or a missing source</h2>
        <p>Found a stale or wrong endorsement, or know an organization we should be tracking?
          Email <a href="mailto:seattle-elections@dobravoda.dev">seattle-elections@dobravoda.dev</a>
          &mdash; no GitHub account needed. If you already use GitHub, you are also welcome to
          open an issue directly against the source repository below.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="who-maintains-this">
        <h2 id="who-maintains-this">Who maintains this</h2>
        <p>This is an independent, volunteer-run project, not affiliated with any campaign,
          party, or any organization it tracks. Its code and methodology are public at
          <a href="{{ project_url }}"{{ external_link_attributes }}>{{ project_url_label }}</a>.</p>
      </section>

    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer">
      {{ shell.footer_band(project_url, shell.footer_audit(data_updated_date, site_updated_date, data_version, git_commit, project_url, data_href)) }}
    </footer>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}
  <script type="module">
{{ shell_entry_script | safe }}
    ShellPage.boot();
  </script>
{% endblock %}
